        "text": "Grandson of Chandragupta Maurya. His inscriptions call him Devanampiya Piyadasi, ‘Beloved of the Gods, of gracious looks’. Eight years after his consecration he conquers Kalinga, then writes of his remorse and turns to Buddhism and dhamma. He never gives up the army, and Kalinga stays in his empire."
