        "text": "No inscription or text names the king who fought Ashoka, or says what became of him. Pliny’s report of 60,000 foot soldiers, 1,000 horsemen and 700 elephants probably describes Kalinga a generation earlier. Whoever he was, his kingdom resisted the strongest army in India hard enough to cost, by Ashoka’s count, 100,000 lives."
